      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A balance is indeed necessary. While communal and social virtues are essential in a democratic society, individual-focused virtues like personal responsibility and self-reliance cannot be overlooked. These traits empower individuals to contribute positively to society, make informed decisions, and lead by example. Being self-governed and accountable encourages personal growth and social cohesion, which are fundamental in modern democratic contexts. Valuing both aspects fosters a harmonious and thriving society.",
